Now record the critique, plus a new uncertainty (U010: component-wise contribution / ablation risk) and update U005.

Let me write the critique.

overall_status: weak_or_flawed.

Let me be careful to make strongest_for fair.

strongest_for: The idea targets a genuine, documented weakness (intermediate supervision missing: C003; RL rewards corrupted: C006); the training-time isolated-vs-context contrast has not been run in the retrieved set (C007), and the closest negative evidence is inference-time prompting on 125 questions over frozen models (C001, C005), which does not measure what gradient updates learn — so a fine-tuning test could genuinely differ. The repair loop has a ready-made operationalization (sub-question correctness, arxiv:2406.13397) and the benchmarks for hop-stratified transfer exist (arxiv:2011.01060, arxiv:2101.03737).

strongest_against: The premise is contradicted in the closest controlled study: holding triple count fixed and swapping all non-chain triples for unrelated material changed F1 by +0.003 (C001), and syntax/order/size were flat (C005). Subgraph retrieval work independently frames extra triples as noise (C002). The two auxiliary claims are pre-empted: intermediate supervision (C003) and reward shaping for corrupted one-hop rewards (C006) already exist, and RL has no reported hop-depth transfer. So even if context enrichment helps, the pipeline is three components each with a strong prior against being the marginal contribution, and the confounders (C009) make a positive result easy to misattribute.

most_important_unresolved_question: Does the +0.003 null for non-chain triples replicate under fine-tuning with passage-coherent (rather than unrelated-entity) context at matched tokens? (U006)

most_dangerous_confounder: token/compute + serialization/order (C009, U007).

closest_paper_ids: arxiv:2609.10237, arxiv:2202.13296, arxiv:2101.03737, doi:10.18653/v1/d18-1362

potential_contribution: If narrowed, the idea could contribute a rigorous negative or boundary result: a token-matched, hop-stratified test of whether passage-coherent context triples change what a fine-tuned LM learns, and whether the inference-time null replicates in training. That is a useful, publishable characterization even if the answer is null — and it requires only the (A) component.

overlap_summary / distinction_summary.

Critique points arrays.

Let me write them.

novelty:
1. {question: "Has essentially the same idea been proposed?", finding: "The manipulation 'put context triples around a target fact and see whether answers improve' is already exercised at inference (arxiv:2609.10237; doi:10.20944/preprints202505.1992.v1) and the subgraph-as-input version is standard (arxiv:2202.13296; doi:10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.99). No retrieved paper runs the training-time isolated-vs-passage-context contrast, so no direct match was found, but the mechanism is a regime change rather than a new mechanism.", severity: "moderate", paper_ids, claim_ids: ["C007"]}
2. {question: "Is the difference only implementation-level?", finding: "Partly. Swapping 'context in the prompt' for 'context in the supervision text' is the main delta over arxiv:2609.10237; if the fine-tuning result matches the prompting null, the idea collapses to an implementation variant of an already-published null. The repair-loop delta over arxiv:2101.03737 is also an implementation choice (regenerate examples vs. learn a teacher distribution).", severity: "high", claim_ids: ["C007","C008"]}

technical_validity:
3. {question:"Does the central premise hold?", finding:"Contradicted in the closest controlled regime: non-chain triples contributed +0.003 F1 and order/size/syntax were flat; subgraph work independently treats extra triples as noise.", severity:"high", paper_ids:["arxiv:2609.10237","arxiv:2202.13296"], claim_ids:["C001","C002","C005"]}
4. {question:"Are the auxiliary components novel or necessary?", finding:"Pre-empted in mechanism: one-hop/intermediate supervision failure is addressed by a bidirectional teacher learning intermediate entity distributions (arxiv:2101.03737) and by embedding-estimated rewards plus edge-mask exploration (doi:10.18653/v1/d18-1362). The idea's detection+example-regeneration loop must beat both.", severity:"high", claim_ids:["C003","C006","C008"]}
5. {question:"Is the RL stage well-posed for deeper-hop transfer?", finding:"RL over incomplete KGs has corrupted one-hop rewards and spurious-path failure modes, and none of the retrieved abstracts reports hop-depth transfer; MetaQA 1/2-hop are already saturated (97.1/99.9), leaving the RL stage little measurable room at low depth.", severity:"moderate", paper_ids:["doi:10.18653/v1/d18-1362","arxiv:2101.03737"], claim_ids:["C006"]}
6. {question:"Is passage provenance technically available?", finding:"Unverified; Freebase-based KBQA pipelines in the retrieved set have no passage notion, so the operational definition of 'same source passage' may fall back to graph neighbourhood and lose the idea's distinguishing feature.", severity:"moderate", paper_ids:["arxiv:2202.13296","arxiv:2011.01060"], claim_ids:["C010"]}

experimental_validity:
7. {question:"Are budgets matched between the two regimes?", finding:"The idea states matching as an assumption, not a design, and the naive isolated-vs-context comparison is confounded by token count; a positive result would be uninterpretable without token-matched random-distractor and unrelated-entity controls of the kind arxiv:2609.10237 uses.", severity:"high", paper_ids:["arxiv:2609.10237"], claim_ids:["C009"]}
8. {question:"Could ordering/serialization produce the claimed result?", finding:"Two papers disagree on whether ordering/serialization matters, so the effect must be isolated by holding order/format fixed; otherwise a gain is attributable to the formatting, not to passage coherence.", severity:"high", paper_ids:["doi:10.20944/preprints202505.1992.v1","arxiv:2609.10237"], claim_ids:["C005","C009"]}
9. {question:"Is there enough headroom to detect an effect?", finding:"Short-hop splits are near-saturated, so the experiment must be pre-registered on 3+ hop / generative-answer splits with reported power.", severity:"moderate", paper_ids:["arxiv:2101.03737","arxiv:2406.13397"], claim_ids:[]}
10. {question:"Are baselines strong and comparable?", finding:"The idea as written names no baselines or base LM; the natural strong baselines are the subgraph reasoners and the teacher-student intermediate-supervision model, which must be run under the same fine-tuning budget.", severity:"moderate", paper_ids:["arxiv:2202.13296","arxiv:2101.03737"], claim_ids:["C007"]}

practicality:
11. {question:"Is the three-stage pipeline feasible within a normal compute budget?", finding:"Three sequential trainings (context fine-tune, iterative repair refinements, RL) each multiply compute, and the gain, if any, is expected on the hardest 3+ hop queries where training is least stable. Running the token-matched controls multiplies it again.", severity:"moderate", claim_ids:["C009"]}
12. {question:"Can the repair loop be built with available signals?", finding:"Detection is assumptive; the most concrete available proxies are sub-question correctness (arxiv:2406.13397) and evidence-path match (arxiv:2011.01060), which require an annotated decomposition not present in every benchmark.", severity:"moderate", paper_ids:["arxiv:2406.13397","arxiv:2011.01060"], claim_ids:["C011"]}

Now record. Also new uncertainty U010 (component-wise ablation / marginal contribution), and update U005 to partially_resolved.

Let me issue record_critique + record_uncertainty U010 + update U005.
